{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall cast.</b> A term of casting, as its Targum renders." "<b>Its corners.</b> As its Targum renders: זִוְיָתֵיהּ; and they were placed on the upper corners, near the cover — two here and two here along the width of the ark, and the poles placed in them, and the length of the ark separated between the poles — a cubit and a half between pole and pole, so that the two men carrying the ark would walk between them; and so it is explained in Menachot, in the chapter Shetei ha-Lechem (Menachot 98)." "<b>And two rings on its one side.</b> These are the very four rings mentioned at the beginning of the verse, and it explains to you where they were; and this ו is extra, and its resolution is like 'two rings' — and you can account for it thus: two of these rings on its one side." "<b>Its side.</b> Its edge."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:26.709547997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}